concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015-sch-1-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 After subsection 115.1(1) of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (1A) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was engaged in before 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on conviction by:  (a) if, at the time the conduct was engaged in, the offence mentioned in paragraph (1)(e) was punishable on conviction by a term of imprisonment (other than imprisonment for life)—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for a term of not more than that term; or  (b) otherwise—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.  (1B) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was engaged in on or after 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on conviction by a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00163  Schedule 1  Amendments  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Harming Australians) Act 2015 No. 163, 2015" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (1A) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was engaged in before 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on conviction by:  (a) if, at the time the conduct was engaged in, the offence mentioned in paragraph (1)(e) was punishable on conviction by a term of imprisonment (other than imprisonment for life)—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for a term of not more than that term; or  (b) otherwise—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.  (1B) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was engaged in on or after 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on conviction by a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00163  Schedule 1  Amendments  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Harming Australians) Act 2015 No. 163, 2015"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "7"^^xsd:integer ;
